# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# onedrive-agent .gitignore
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Agent run logs -- generated locally each run, never committed.
# Each run produces a timestamped file in logs/ -- these are for
# local monitoring and diagnosis only, not source control.
logs/

# Python cache -- auto-generated by Python, not source files.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo

# Environment / secrets -- belt-and-suspenders protection.
# The API keys are stored as Windows environment variables (never
# in files), but this ensures that even if someone accidentally
# creates a .env file locally, it won't be committed.
.env
*.env

# OS-generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# VS Code / editor settings (local preferences, not project config)
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude Code local permissions -- machine-specific, never versioned.
.claude/settings.local.json

pre_run_snapshot.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Privacy: raw live-run scan output (added 2026-08-02)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The live-run phases scan real personal folders. Raw scan output
# contains the full path of every file scanned, which discloses --
# by folder and filename alone -- employment dispute records,
# firearm licence records, identity and estate documents, medical
# scheme membership and third-party names. This repo is public.
#
# Sanitized, aggregate-only versions of these artefacts are
# committed instead; see sanitize_repo_artifacts.py. These raw
# files stay local.
sanitize_mapping.json
robocopy_backup_log.txt
*_RAW.json
*_DELTA_RAW.json

# Pre-sanitisation originals, retained locally for reference only.
_raw_local_only/

# Local-only audit helpers, never committed.
_audit_*.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Git bundles / history backups (added 2026-08-02, RAID I27)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Pre-purge backup bundles contain the COMPLETE original history,
# including every personal path and the ID-formatted number that were
# deliberately purged from this repo. Committing one would silently undo
# the entire remediation.
#
# The pre-commit guard CANNOT protect against this: bundle contents are
# zlib-compressed, so text scanning sees nothing. Verified -- staging a
# bundle full of the purged data returns "CLEAN". This ignore rule is the
# only control.
#
# These backups should ideally live OUTSIDE the repository entirely.
*.bundle
*.pack
PurgeGItHPrivateData/
